>> title: Mantecadas
>> category: Cakes & Loaves
>> tags: butter, vanilla, mexican, muffin, oven
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: mantecada, mantecadas, mantecadas de vainilla, mexican muffin, panqué individual, panque individual, cupcake de panadería
>> pairs-with: conchas
>> servings: 12
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: cream 4 min
>> step.2: beat in the eggs and vanilla
>> step.3: fold in the dry and the milk, alternating
>> step.4: scoop into 12 fluted cases
>> step.5: bake 5 min hot, then 13 min at 350°F

Cream @softened unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g) with @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g) ~cream{4%min} until it is pale and holds a ribbon.

Beat @eggs{2%large}(100 g), one at a time, and @vanilla extract{2%tsp}(10 mL) into @&(~1)creamed butter{}.

Add @all-purpose flour{1 3/4%cup}(210 g), @baking powder{2%tsp}(8 g) and @table salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g) to @&(~1)batter{} in three goes, alternating with @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), and stop the moment the last flour disappears.

Scoop @&(~1)finished batter{} into 12 fluted paper cases set in a muffin #tin{}, filling each three-quarters full — the paper case is the item, and a mantecada is served in it.

Bake @&(~1)filled cases{} at 400°F ~blast{5%min} to throw the dome up, then drop the oven to 350°F and ~bake{13%min} until a skewer comes out clean.
